                "You want to show the other side that the photo, article, or video you made is genuine and unaltered.",
              stepsLabel: "What you do (issuing)",
              steps: [
                "Decide what to prove (author, capture time, unedited, and so on)",
                "Issue with provenance and a signature attached, without handing over the source data",
                "Deliver only the proof to the receiver",
              ],
              lemma: `Attaching provenance and issuing is <a href="${L("/seal/")}">Seal</a>. It works alongside C2PA (Coalition for Content Provenance and Authenticity).`,
              ctaLabel: "See how to start issuing →",
              ctaHref: L("/seal/"),
            },
            {
              kind: "receive",
              tag: "Receiver",
              role: "Receiver side",
              sub: "You receive and use content",
              actors: [
                "Distribution platforms",
                "Advertisers & agencies",
                "Downstream reusers",
                "Verifying AI agents",
              ],
              problem:
                "You want to confirm beforehand that the image or article you received is genuine and from a legitimate issuer.",
              stepsLabel: "What you do (verifying)",
              steps: [
                "Receive the attached proof",
                "Verify the issuer and whether it was altered (without opening the contents)",
                "Use or distribute only what checks out",
              ],
              lemma: `Verification is <a href="${L("/pillars/verifiable-ai/")}">Verifiable AI (Pillar 02)</a> and <a href="${L("/pillars/verifiable-origin/")}">Verifiable Origin (Pillar 01)</a>. You receive only the proof.`,
              ctaLabel: "See how to start verifying →",
              ctaHref: L("/pillars/verifiable-ai/"),
              ctaExtra: `for the technical detail, see <a href="#verify">“How to verify authenticity”</a> below`,
            },
          ],
          note: "Layer Lemma's cryptographic verification on top of the standards (C2PA / W3C VC). Issuing and verifying are a pair — the same provenance, handled from both sides.",
        },
        {
          id: "verify",
          label: "How to verify authenticity",
          h2: "How to verify authenticity",
          body: ["The technologies that support authenticity divide into several layers."],
          list: [
            "<strong>Electronic signatures</strong>: show that the author is who they claim and that nothing was altered after signing.",
            "<strong>Timestamps</strong>: fix when something existed.",
            "<strong>Hashes</strong>: check whether contents match.",
            "<strong>Provenance</strong>: record the chain of who created or edited what, when, and where. C2PA is the standard for attaching this provenance to content.",
            "<strong>Zero-knowledge proofs (ZK proofs)</strong>: prove only that a condition is met, without disclosing the underlying data.",
          ],
          after: [
            `The key point is that <strong>detection and proof are different things</strong>. Detection — finding anomalies after the fact — is indispensable for grasping damage. But detection does not establish, before the fact, whether the data in hand is genuine and came from a legitimate origin. Finding an anomaly afterward does not stop a process that has already gone through. Authenticity is upheld only when there is a layer that <strong>independently verifies provenance before execution</strong> (see <a href="${L("/blog/detection-is-not-proof/")}">detection is not proof</a>).`,
          ],
        },
        {
          id: "lemma",
          label: "Lemma's provenance proof",
          h2: "Meet authenticity with Lemma's provenance proof",
          body: [
            "Lemma proves provenance without handing over the data. The source data never goes to Lemma; what you receive is only a proof that the provenance is traceable.",
          ],
          list: [
            "<strong>Cryptographically verified provenance</strong>: fixes who created which version, when, and whether it was altered, as a tamper-proof proof.",
            "<strong>Prove without exposing data</strong>: zero-knowledge proofs show only authenticity without disclosing the source data. <strong>Selective disclosure</strong> reveals only the attributes you need, minimally.",
            "<strong>Works alongside standards</strong>: designed to cooperate with C2PA, MCP, A2A, and x402. It does not replace content provenance standards — it layers verification on top of them.",
            "<strong>Model-independent</strong>: even when AI models change, the provenance proof remains.",
          ],
          after: [
            `For the design, see <a href="${L("/pillars/verifiable-origin/")}">Verifiable Origin (Pillar 01)</a> and <a href="${L("/seal/")}">Seal</a>; for verifying AI output, see <a href="${L("/pillars/verifiable-ai/")}">Verifiable AI (Pillar 02)</a> and <a href="${L("/trust402/")}">Trust402</a>.`,
          ],
        },
      ],
      faqLabel: "Frequently asked questions",
      faq: [
        {
          q: "What is the difference between authenticity and integrity?",
          a: "Integrity guarantees that the content has not been altered. Authenticity adds to that whether the origin is genuine — who made it and that it is not an impersonation — a broader concept.",
        },
        {
          q: "What does authenticity mean under e-record and medical-record rules?",
          a: "That a record is genuine, that any alteration or deletion is traceable, and that the author's responsibility is clear. It is upheld through electronic signatures, timestamps, and operation history (provenance). In Japanese e-records it is one of three requirements: authenticity, legibility, and preservation.",
        },
        {
          q: "How does C2PA relate to provenance proof?",
          a: "C2PA is an industry standard for attaching provenance information to content. Lemma's provenance proof works alongside it, providing the layer that cryptographically verifies the attached provenance. It is complementary, not a replacement.",
        },
        {
          q: "Can detection tools alone protect authenticity?",
          a: "Detection finds anomalies after the fact and is indispensable for grasping damage. But it does not establish, before execution, whether something came from a genuine origin. Authenticity needs a layer that independently verifies provenance beforehand.",
        },
      ],
      referencesLabel: "Primary sources",
      references: [
        {
          n: 1,
          text: "National Tax Agency — Electronic Books Maintenance system special site (電子帳簿保存法, in Japanese)",
          url: "https://www.nta.go.jp/law/joho-zeikaishaku/sonota/jirei/tokusetsu/index.htm",
        },
        {
          n: 2,
          text: "Ministry of Health, Labour and Welfare — Guidelines for the Safety Management of Medical Information Systems, ed. 6.0 (in Japanese)",
          url: "https://www.mhlw.go.jp/stf/shingi/0000516275_00006.html",
        },
        {
          n: 3,
          text: "C2PA (Coalition for Content Provenance and Authenticity) — official site & technical specifications",
          url: "https://c2pa.org/",
        },
      ],
      ctaLabel: "Next step",
      ctaH2: "Build authenticity into the decisions that matter",
      ctaBody:
        "How should you design for authenticity in your own operations? We will talk through what changes with Lemma in a 30-minute Discovery Call. You do not need to disclose any source data.",
      ctaItems: [
        {
          label: "A data foundation for delegating work to AI safely",
          desc: "How to prove authenticity without handing over data, and how to adopt it.",
          href: anshinUrl,
        },
        {
          label: "Discovery Call (30 min)",
          desc: "Start from a conversation. Get in touch.",
          href: discoveryUrl,
        },
        {
          label: "Lemma Critical Weekly",
          desc: "A structural analysis of real risk incidents, in your inbox each week.",
          href: newsletterUrl,
        },
        {
          label: "See the cases — Lemma Critical Briefs",
          desc: "Read real breaks of authenticity, structurally.",
          href: L("/critical/briefs/"),
        },
      ],
    };

const articleJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  headline: C.h1,
  description: C.metaDescription,
  url: pageUrl,
  inLanguage: locale,
  author: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Lemma" },
  publisher: {
    "@type": "Organization",
    name: "Lemma",
    logo: { "@type": "ImageObject", url: `${SITE}/favicon.svg` },
  },
  mainEntityOfPage: { "@type": "WebPage", "@id": pageUrl },
  about: [
    { "@type": "Thing", name: isJa ? "真正性" : "Authenticity" },
    { "@type": "Thing", name: isJa ? "データ来歴" : "Data provenance" },
  ],
};

const faqJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  mainEntity: C.faq.map((item) => ({
    "@type": "Question",
    name: item.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: item.a },
  })),
};

const breadcrumbJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  itemListElement: [
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      position: 1,
      name: C.breadcrumbHome,
      item: `${SITE}${base || "/"}`,
    },
    { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: C.breadcrumbHere, item: pageUrl },
  ],
};
---

<Layout
  locale={locale}
  title={C.metaTitle}
  description={C.metaDescription}
  metaType="page"
  pagePath="/authenticity/"
>
  <script
    type="application/ld+json"
    is:inline
    set:html={JSON.stringify(articleJsonLd)}
  />
  <script
    type="application/ld+json"
    is:inline
    set:html={JSON.stringify(faqJsonLd)}
  />
  <script
    type="application/ld+json"
    is:inline
    set:html={JSON.stringify(breadcrumbJsonLd)}
  />
  <Navigation locale={locale} t={t.nav} base={base} />
  <HubSpotDrawer />

  <main class="au-page">
    <div class="au-container">
      <article>
        <header class="au-hero">
          <div class="au-eyebrow">{C.eyebrow}</div>
          <h1 class="au-h1">{C.h1}</h1>
          {C.intro.map((p) => <p class="au-lead" set:html={p} />)}
        </header>

        <nav class="au-jump" aria-label={C.eyebrow}>
          <div class="au-jump-inner">
            {C.sections.map((s, i) => (
              <a
                href={`#${s.id}`}
                class={`au-jump-pill${i === 0 ? " is-active" : ""}`}
                data-jump-target={s.id}
              >
                {s.label}
              </a>
            ))}
          </div>
        </nav>

        {C.sections.map((s) =>
          s.variant === "lanes" ? (
            <section class="au-section au-lanes" id={s.id} data-section>
              <div class="au-section-label">{s.label}</div>
              <h2 class="au-h2">{s.h2}</h2>
              <p class="au-p" set:html={s.intro} />
              <div class="au-lane-grid">
                {s.lanes.map((ln) => (
                  <section
                    class={`au-lane${ln.kind === "receive" ? " au-lane--receive" : ""}`}
                  >
                    <span class="au-lane-tag">{ln.tag}</span>
                    <div class="au-lane-role">{ln.role}</div>
                    <div class="au-lane-sub">{ln.sub}</div>
                    <div class="au-lane-actors">
                      {ln.actors.map((a) => (
                        <span class="au-lane-actor">{a}</span>
                      ))}
                    </div>
                    <p class="au-lane-problem">{ln.problem}</p>
                    <div class="au-lane-lead">{ln.stepsLabel}</div>
                    <ol class="au-lane-steps">
                      {ln.steps.map((st) => (
                        <li>{st}</li>
                      ))}
                    </ol>
                    <p class="au-lane-lemma" set:html={ln.lemma} />
                    <a class="au-lane-cta" href={ln.ctaHref}>
                      {ln.ctaLabel}
                    </a>
                    {ln.ctaExtra && (
                      <p class="au-lane-extra" set:html={ln.ctaExtra} />
                    )}
                  </section>
                ))}
              </div>
              <p class="au-lane-note">{s.note}</p>
            </section>
          ) : (
            <section class="au-section" id={s.id} data-section>
              <div class="au-section-label">{s.label}</div>
              <h2 class="au-h2">{s.h2}</h2>
              {s.body.map((p) => <p class="au-p" set:html={p} />)}
              <ul class="au-list">
                {s.list.map((li) => <li set:html={li} />)}
              </ul>
              {s.after.map((p) => <p class="au-p" set:html={p} />)}
            </section>
          ),
        )}

        <section class="au-section" id="faq" data-section>
          <div class="au-section-label">{C.faqLabel}</div>
          <h2 class="au-h2">{C.faqLabel}</h2>
          <dl class="au-faq">
            {C.faq.map((item) => (
              <div class="au-faq-item">
                <dt class="au-faq-q">{item.q}</dt>
                <dd class="au-faq-a">{item.a}</dd>
              </div>
            ))}
          </dl>
        </section>

        <section class="au-section au-refs" id="references">
          <div class="au-section-label">{C.referencesLabel}</div>
          <ol class="au-ref-list">
            {C.references.map((r) => (
              <li id={`ref-${r.n}`}>
                <a href={r.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{r.text}</a>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ol>
        </section>
      </article>

      <!-- CTA -->
      <section class="au-cta" aria-label={C.ctaLabel}>
        <div class="au-cta-eyebrow">{C.ctaLabel}</div>
        <h2 class="au-cta-h2">{C.ctaH2}</h2>
        <p class="au-cta-body">{C.ctaBody}</p>
        <div class="au-cta-grid">
          {C.ctaItems.map((item) => (
            <a
              class="au-cta-card"
              href={item.href}
              target={item.href.startsWith("http") ? "_blank" : undefined}
              rel={item.href.startsWith("http") ? "noopener" : undefined}
            >
              <span class="au-cta-card-title">{item.label}</span>
              <span class="au-cta-card-desc">{item.desc}</span>
              <span class="au-cta-card-arrow">→</span>
            </a>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer locale={locale} t={t.nav} footerT={t.footer} base={base} />
</Layout>

<style>
  .au-page {
    --au-display: "Sora", system-ui, sans-serif;
    --au-body: "Noto Sans JP", "Sora", system-ui, sans-serif;
    --au-mono: "Space Mono", ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    --au-text-1: #1a1a1a;
    --au-text-2: #3a3a3a;
    --au-text-3: #5a5a5a;
    --au-text-4: #9a9a9a;
    background: var(--lemma-cream);
    color: var(--au-text-2);
    font-family: var(--au-body);
    line-height: 1.85;
    padding: 0 0 32px;
    margin-top: 64px;
  }
  :root[lang="en"] .au-page {
    --au-body: "Sora", system-ui, sans-serif;
  }
  .au-container {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 40px;
  }

  /* ─── HERO ─── */
  .au-hero {
    padding: 64px 0 36px;
  }
  .au-eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--au-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.32em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin: 0 0 22px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  .au-eyebrow::before {
    content: "";
    width: 28px;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--accent);
  }
  .au-h1 {
    font-family: var(--au-display);
    font-size: 52px;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.08;
    color: var(--black);
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    margin: 0 0 24px;
  }
  :root[lang="ja"] .au-h1 {
    font-size: 42px;
    line-height: 1.22;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }
  .au-lead {
    font-size: 16.5px;
    color: var(--au-text-1);
    line-height: 1.9;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }

  /* ─── STICKY JUMP NAV ─── */
  .au-jump {
    position: sticky;
    top: 64px;
    z-index: 5;
    background: var(--lemma-cream);
    padding: 10px 0;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    border-top: 0.5px solid var(--lemma-line);
    border-bottom: 0.5px solid var(--lemma-line);
  }
  .au-jump-inner {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: nowrap;
    gap: 6px;
    overflow-x: auto;
    scrollbar-width: none;
    padding: 2px 0;
  }
  .au-jump-inner::-webkit-scrollbar {
    display: none;
  }
  .au-jump-pill {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    font-family: var(--au-display);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--au-text-3);
    background: var(--white);
    border: 0.5px solid var(--lemma-line);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 7px 14px;
    text-decoration: none;
    white-space: nowrap;
    transition: color 0.15s, border-color 0.15s, background 0.15s;
  }
  .au-jump-pill:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
    border-color: rgba(139, 69, 19, 0.4);
  }
  .au-jump-pill.is-active {
    color: var(--lemma-cream);
    background: var(--accent);
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }

  /* ─── SECTIONS ─── */
  .au-section {
    padding: 36px 0;
    border-top: 0.5px solid var(--lemma-line);
    scroll-margin-top: 140px;
  }
  .au-section-label {
    font-family: var(--au-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.28em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }
  .au-h2 {
    font-family: var(--au-display);
    font-size: 28px;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--black);
    margin: 0 0 18px;
  }
  :root[lang="ja"] .au-h2 {
    font-size: 25px;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }
  .au-p {
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--au-text-2);
    line-height: 1.9;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }
  .au-p a,
  .au-list a,
  .au-lead a {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .au-p a:hover,
  .au-list a:hover,
  .au-lead a:hover {
    color: #6e3610;
  }
  .au-list {
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .au-list li {
    position: relative;
    padding: 0 0 0 22px;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.85;
    color: var(--au-text-2);
  }
  .au-list li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 12px;
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent);
  }
  .au-list li strong {
    color: var(--black);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  /* ─── ISSUER / RECEIVER LANES ─── */
  .au-lanes .au-h2 {
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .au-lane-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 20px;
    margin: 22px 0 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .au-lane-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
  /* Flat, no-radius cards, top-edge accent per lane (issue=brown, receive=black). */
  .au-lane {
    background: #f5f5f5;
    border: none;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 0;
    padding: 32px 30px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  .au-lane--receive {
    border-top-color: var(--black);
  }
  .au-lane-tag {
    font-family: var(--au-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .au-lane--receive .au-lane-tag {
    color: var(--black);
  }
  .au-lane-role {
    font-family: var(--au-display);
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--black);
    line-height: 1.25;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .au-lane-sub {
    font-size: 13.5px;
    color: var(--au-text-3);
    margin-top: 4px;
  }
  .au-lane-actors {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
    margin: 16px 0 18px;
  }
  .au-lane-actor {
    font-family: var(--au-mono);
    font-size: 11.5px;
    color: var(--accent);
    background: #f5efe6;
    padding: 5px 11px;
    border-radius: 0;
  }
  .au-lane--receive .au-lane-actor {
    color: #1a1a1a;
    background: #e8e8e8;
  }
  .au-lane-problem {
    font-size: 14.5px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--au-text-1);
    margin: 0 0 18px;
  }
  .au-lane-lead {
    font-family: var(--au-mono);
    font-size: 10.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--au-text-4);
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .au-lane-steps {
    font-size: 14.5px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--au-text-1);
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    padding-left: 1.3em;
  }
  .au-lane-steps li {
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .au-lane-lemma {
    font-size: 13.5px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--au-text-2);
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }
  .au-lane-lemma a,
  .au-lane-extra a {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .au-lane-cta {
    font-family: var(--au-display);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
    margin-top: auto;
  }
  .au-lane--receive .au-lane-cta {
    color: var(--black);
  }
  .au-lane-cta:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  .au-lane-extra {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--au-text-3);
    margin: 8px 0 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .au-lane-note {
    margin: 20px 0 0;
    padding: 18px 22px;
    background: var(--white);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--lemma-line);
    font-size: 13.5px;
    color: var(--au-text-2);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  /* ─── FAQ ─── */
  .au-faq {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .au-faq-item {
    padding: 18px 0;
    border-bottom: 0.5px solid var(--lemma-line);
  }
  .au-faq-item:first-child {
    border-top: 0.5px solid var(--lemma-line);
  }
  .au-faq-q {
    font-family: var(--au-display);
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--black);
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin: 0 0 8px;
  }
  .au-faq-a {
    font-size: 14.5px;
    color: var(--au-text-2);
    line-height: 1.85;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ─── REFERENCES (footnotes) ─── */
  .au-ref {
    font-size: 0.7em;
    line-height: 0;
    margin-left: 1px;
  }
  .au-ref a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .au-ref-list {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0 0 0 20px;
  }
  .au-ref-list li {
